{"name":"Bubblegum Crisis","hex":"#eeccee","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bubblegum","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sweet, stretchable chewing gum designed for blowing bubbles.","A type of pop music marked by sweetness, pep and charm (rather than depth or complexity)."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Tasting like bubblegum.","Sweet, perky, or youthful."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bubblegum"},{"term":"crisis","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A crucial or decisive point or situation; a turning point.","An unstable situation, in political, social, economic or military affairs, especially one involving an impending abrupt change."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crisis"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bubblegum Crisis","blocks":[{"text":"Bubblegum Crisis  is a 1987–1991 Japanese cyberpunk original video animation (OVA) series produced by Youmex and animated by AIC and Artmic. Set in the year 2032, seven years after a massive earthquake devastates Tokyo, the story centers on the reconstruction of the city under the influence of the megacorporation Genom, which mass-produces bio-organic androids called Boomers for labor and defense. When Boomers begin malfunctioning and rampaging through the city, the Knight Sabers surface as an all-female quartet of mercenaries who use advanced powered suits to combat rogue Boomers. The success of the series spawned multiple sequel and prequel series, as well as a reboot."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c1/BGC_OVA.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bubblegum_Crisis","wikidata":"Q997465"},{"title":"Bubblegum Crisis (role-playing game)","blocks":[{"text":"Bubblegum Crisis is a near-future cyberpunk role-playing game published by R. Talsorian Games in 1996 that is based on the anime television series Bubblegum Crisis."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/fe/Bubblegum_Crisis%2C_role-playing_game.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bubblegum_Crisis_(role-playing_game)","wikidata":"Q2927394"},{"title":"Bubble gum","blocks":[{"text":"Bubble gum is a type of chewing gum, designed to be inflated out of the mouth as a bubble."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Blowing_bubble_gum.jpg/330px-Blowing_bubble_gum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bubble_gum","wikidata":"Q1318753"},{"title":"Crisis","blocks":[{"text":"A crisis is any event or period that will lead to an unstable and dangerous situation affecting an individual, group, or all of society. Crises are negative changes in the human or environmental affairs, especially when they occur abruptly, with little or no warning. More loosely, a crisis is a testing time for an emergency."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/EXCOMM_meeting%2C_Cuban_Missile_Crisis%2C_29_October_1962.jpg/330px-EXCOMM_meeting%2C_Cuban_Missile_Crisis%2C_29_October_1962.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crisis","wikidata":"Q381072"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c1/BGC_OVA.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c1/BGC_OVA.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABGC_OVA.png"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/fe/Bubblegum_Crisis%2C_role-playing_game.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/fe/Bubblegum_Crisis%2C_role-playing_game.j